# Archways - BONANZA's ARCHWAY test course (SPEC.md 130.39), built only by the BZARCH=1 knob, as water.bbc is by
# BZWATER=1.  NOT a shipped course: the knob adds it to BZ_COURSES after the shipped ones and makes it the
# pathway's pad 0, so a new game rests on it (title, Play Game, Enter).  Not on the TOUR.
#
# Everything is at 2 units.  An archway is a CEILING the ball rolls under: a ball in the air above its clearance
# meets its face as a wall, and inside it the underside stops a rise.
#  - S, the start plate, with a RUBBER pad and a GLASS pad;
#  - A, a one-cell path along x, a 2-unit ARCHWAY over a STEEL PAD at its middle: rubber cannot boost over the
#    pad - the arch's face stops it - so it rolls through and leaves as steel;
#  - T, the plate at A's end, a RUBBER pad on it (to try B as rubber again);
#  - B, a one-cell path along y down from T, a bare 2-unit archway: Hop and boost into it and the ball hits;
#    exit 0 on the plate G below it;
#  - C, a TWO-WIDE path along x off T's right, a 3-unit two-wide archway the ball rolls through (a Hop passes
#    under a 3-unit underside); exit 1 at its end goes on to FIRST.
course ARCH "Archways"
width  128
ball rubber
uses archway

floor rect 4 4 8 9 flat 2   # S, the start plate
floor rect 8 6 18 7 flat 2   # A, the one-cell path
floor rect 18 4 22 11 flat 2   # T, the plate at A's end
floor rect 20 11 21 18 flat 2   # B, the one-cell path down from T
floor rect 18 18 23 22 flat 2   # G, the plate below B
floor rect 22 6 31 8 flat 2   # C, the two-wide path off T

archway tile 12 6 along x   # A's arch over the steel pad (2 units: rubber's boost hits it)
archway tile 20 14 along y   # B's bare arch (2 units)
archway rect 25 6 26 8 along x under 3   # C's two-wide arch (3 units: a Hop passes under)

pad rubber 5 5
pad glass 5 7
pad steel 12 6
pad rubber 19 9
start 6 6
goal tile 20 20 flat 2
goal rect 30 6 31 8 flat 2 exit 1
clock 22 20
clock 29 6
target 60
way 6 6
way 11 6
way 17 6
way 20 7
way 20 11
way 20 17
way 20 20
